&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE COMPANY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Juul Labs&#39;s mission is to transition the world’s billion adult smokers away from combustible cigarettes, eliminate their use, and combat underage usage of our products. We have the opportunity to address one of the world’s most intractable challenges through a commitment to exceptional quality, research, design, and innovation. Backed by leading technology investors, we are committed to the same excellence when it comes to hiring great talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a diverse team that is united by this common purpose and we are hiring the world’s best engineers, scientists, designers, product managers, operations experts, and customer service and business professionals. If the opportunity to build your career is compelling, read on for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on the AI Software Team across all areas of our global software infrastructure: e-commerce frontend &amp;amp; backend, connected device application integrations, enterprise application integrations, third-party logistics integrations, access controls &amp;amp; regulatory compliance, customer service, and any other supported infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for development and release to production for all assigned work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for investigation and resolution of production issues in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend regular team meeting cadences to communicate and drive clarity on assigned work and team planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build expertise in Ruby, Rails, TypeScript, and NextJS as needed to be a productive member of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development lead, fellow software engineers, and product managers to deliver assigned work and shaping our future roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PERSONAL AND PROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of successfully shipping complex components and web application systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and designing APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and deep understanding of web application reliability, performance, scalability, and error handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and/or mentoring a team of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge or willingness to learn the following technologies:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTML/CSS/Javascript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React &amp;amp; NextJS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ruby on Rails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Postgres&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS + Terraform or Pulumi&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vercel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years of experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EDUCATION:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or higher in Computer Science or equivalent experience in Web Application development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JUUL LABS PERKS &amp;amp; BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A place to grow your career. We’ll help you set big goals - and exceed them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People. Work with talented, committed and supportive teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity and performance bonuses. Every employee is a stakeholder in our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cell phone subsidy, commuter benefits and discounts on JUUL products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent medical, dental and vision, disability, and life insurance, plus family support, wellness, legal, and employee assistance program benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus biannual discretionary performance bonuses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Juul Labs is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive work environment for all employees and job applicants, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, gender identity or gender expression, national origin, disability or veteran status. We will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance. Juul Labs also complies with the employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration and Nationality Act. All applicants must have authorization to work for Juul Labs in the US.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SALARY RANGES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Salary varies by role, level and location, and is dependent on the cost of labor in a given&lt;br&gt;geographic region among other factors. These ranges may be modified at any time.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;SALARY RANGE:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$127,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$159,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE COMPANY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Juul Labs&#39;s mission is to transition the world’s billion adult smokers away from combustible cigarettes, eliminate their use, and combat underage usage of our products. We have the opportunity to address one of the world’s most intractable challenges through a commitment to exceptional quality, research, design, and innovation. Backed by leading technology investors, we are committed to the same excellence when it comes to hiring great talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a diverse team that is united by this common purpose and we are hiring the world’s best engineers, scientists, designers, product managers, operations experts, and customer service and business professionals. If the opportunity to build your career is compelling, read on for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JUUL is the market leader in the e-Cigarette category with a tremendous amount of growth potential within our US Commercial organization. This is an exciting opportunity to continue the expansion of our national accounts’ state of the business as we roll out new brand strategy in non-convenience channels in drug, grocery and value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Key Account Manager role will demand excellence, attention to detail and responsibility for being the primary point person representing Juul with the nicotine category teams of Walgreen’s and British Petroleum portfolio of c-stores. The successful candidate will need to build trust, identify growth opportunities, communicate detailed tactics and strategies, and provide excellent account knowledge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this role, the ideal candidate should be self-sufficient and highly capable in on-boarding and managing large format chain accounts at the HQ level. Having previous experience calling on the HQ level of one of these accounts is favored.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote-based role: Preferred states KY, OH or IL&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in facilitating and managing buyer meetings, category review and analysis, T2T’s contracted space, and inventory resolution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely and detailed internal and external communications to all stakeholders involved in the management and success of driving growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience distilling actionable insights from complex data and explaining findings to stakeholders in a digestible and compelling manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver successful retail programming partnerships, contract partnerships and campaigns that maximize ROI and provide win-win outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively communicate with internal department leads, retail and distribution contacts to develop &amp;amp; execute sales strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform related duties as assigned, within your scope of practice&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRAVEL AND OPERATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is field-based and requires regular travel, estimated at an average of 40% of work hours, though this may fluctuate based on business needs. Travel includes the operation of a motor vehicle and/or commercial air travel and will necessitate overnight stays. Essential travel activities include conducting quarterly business reviews, broker meetings, HQ planning sessions, sponsored events, market/store visits, and internal in-person meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must possess and maintain a valid U.S. driver&#39;s license in good standing for a minimum of the last three (3) consecutive years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable vehicle or willingness to obtain a vehicle that can be used for work daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PERSONAL AND PROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5 years related work experience in account management at HQ level of large format retail or distribution in CPG&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and problem-solving abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter and ability to work and deliver results in a remote-working environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced, cross-functional, entrepreneurial environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient using technology software and CRM (PowerPoint, Excel, Salesforce, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous work experience in a regulated industry, specifically tobacco products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EDUCATION:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing or other related business fields, or five years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JUUL LABS PERKS &amp;amp; BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A place to grow your career. We’ll help you set big goals - and exceed them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People. Work with talented, committed and supportive teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity and performance bonuses. Every employee is a stakeholder in our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cell phone subsidy, commuter benefits and discounts on JUUL products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent medical, dental and vision, disability, and life insurance, plus family support, wellness, legal, and employee assistance program benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus biannual discretionary performance bonuses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Juul Labs is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive work environment for all employees and job applicants, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, gender identity or gender expression, national origin, disability or veteran status. We will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance. Juul Labs also complies with the employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration and Nationality Act. All applicants must have authorization to work for Juul Labs in the US. #LI-remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SALARY RANGES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Salary varies by role, level and location, and is dependent on the cost of labor in a given&lt;br&gt;geographic region among other factors. These ranges may be modified at any time.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;SALARY RANGE:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$94,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$119,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE COMPANY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Juul Labs&#39;s mission is to transition the world’s billion adult smokers away from combustible cigarettes, eliminate their use, and combat underage usage of our products. We have the opportunity to address one of the world’s most intractable challenges through a commitment to exceptional quality, research, design, and innovation. Backed by leading technology investors, we are committed to the same excellence when it comes to hiring great talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a diverse team that is united by this common purpose and we are hiring the world’s best engineers, scientists, designers, product managers, operations experts, and customer service and business professionals. If the opportunity to build your career is compelling, read on for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Field Sales, the Senior City Development Manager is the lead field operator for key strategic cities. Bringing strong commercial experience, this hands-on role combines city strategy, regional key account management, and specialist product knowledge to ensure field activity is tailored, scaled, and executed effectively. As well as taking primary ownership of their own city performance - driving awareness, distribution, trade execution, and market share - the role provides commercial coaching and practical support to City Development Managers across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Delivery &amp;amp; Strategic Customer Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account Management: Take ownership of regional key account operators and on-the-ground route-to-market partnerships. Build strong commercial relationships that drive long-term growth across distribution, execution, education, and rate-of-sale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Coaching: Act as a commercial sounding board for City Development Managers. Offer practical advice, coaching, and support on account planning, negotiating, and working through local trade challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Tools: Create, refine, and deploy practical commercial sales tools (e.g., commercial calculators, regional activity, customer and channel propositions) that address ground-level field challenges and help field teams and CDMs win across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional Development: Build relationships and develop non-traditional trade channels, tailoring the approach to fit local market nuances while ensuring all partnerships align with company goals and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution Standards&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Set the operational benchmark for distribution, brand visibility, and advocacy across all trade channels (including priority regional accounts, Wholesale, Vape, and alternative channels). Measure and evaluate execution quality across key cities, establishing clear guidelines and sharing proven approaches to help CDMs elevate standards across their own territories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;City Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;City Strategy: Adapt national frameworks into practical, city-specific plans that reflect local demographics, trade setups, and regional key account footprints. Identify what each specific city needs to win, ensuring resources are deployed effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CDM Guidance: support CDMs in analysing their own cities, adapting national plans to fit their city&#39;s specific dynamics, and executing tailored activity efficiently.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Third-Party Prioritisation: Work alongside and co-ordinate third-party field teams on a city-by-city basis, making sure field resources are directed to where the local opportunity is greatest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Events &amp;amp; Activations: Identify and execute local promotional activity and trade programmes, designed specifically around the local target audience to drive engagement, product education, and sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Ownership: drive city performance and manage risks and opportunities in your region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field Insight &amp;amp; Strategy: Link field execution with the Head of Field Sales by translating plans into action, while feeding back trade realities, competitor moves, and new channel opportunities to shape national strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR PROFILE: Personal and Professional Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years’ experience in a similar role or commercial setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Acumen &amp;amp; Account Management: Strong track record in account management alongside experience handling multi-site accounts that span across adjacent territories. Proven ability to negotiate, drive sales volume, distribution, and market share. Ability to adapt style to both existing and new channels and opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Coaching &amp;amp; Regional Influence: Proven ability to influence and mentor peers by sharing commercial expertise, guiding regional key account negotiations, and helping tailor city plans, all while supporting established line-management structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Tools: Experience developing practical sales tools and toolkits to solve local trade challenges and drive regional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Quality Evaluation: Skilled at turning ideas into reality by tailoring local activations, brand, and direct engagement opportunities to fit specific city needs. Proven ability to measure and evaluate sales return, and &lt;strong&gt;provide analysis to inform future &lt;/strong&gt;execution standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Analysis &amp;amp; Problem Solving: Skilled at analysing city sales data and trade trends to spot commercial gaps, fix underperforming territories, and feed clear market feedback to the Head of Field Sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-Driven &amp;amp; Resilient: Challenges the status quo, takes decisive action, and turns ideas into commercial results in changing environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A full UK driving licence is required for this role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: BA/BS degree preferred but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JUUL LABS PERKS &amp;amp; BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A place to grow your career. We’ll help you set big goals - and exceed them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People. Work with talented, committed and supportive teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity and performance bonuses. Every employee is a stakeholder in our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location. Field based with a requirement to be in the London office when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Juul Labs is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive work environment for all employees and job applicants, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, gender identity or gender expression, national origin, disability or veteran status. We will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance. Juul Labs also complies with the employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration and Nationality Act. All applicants must have authorization to work for Juul Labs in the US.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE COMPANY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Juul Labs&#39;s mission is to transition the world’s billion adult smokers away from combustible cigarettes, eliminate their use, and combat underage usage of our products. We have the opportunity to address one of the world’s most intractable challenges through a commitment to exceptional quality, research, design, and innovation. Backed by leading technology investors, we are committed to the same excellence when it comes to hiring great talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;We are a diverse team that is united by this common purpose and we are hiring the world’s best engineers, scientists, designers, product managers, operations experts, and customer service and business professionals. If the opportunity to build your career is compelling, read on for more details.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The Senior Manager, Commercial Capabilities is a hands-on leader responsible for managing and optimizing the tools and platforms that support the US Commercial organization. Reporting to the Sr. Director, Commercial Planning &amp;amp; PMO, this role is focused on CRM administration and roadmap ownership for Commercial technology improvements. The Senior Manager will work closely with Commercial leadership, IT, and external vendors to maintain and enhance our Commercial technologies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate brings either solid software engineering experience applied to Commercial systems, or strong process operations skills with hands-on experience in enterprise technology platforms — paired in both cases with cross-functional collaboration skills and the ability to lead a small team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Commercial Systems Operations &amp;amp; Planning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and contribute to the Commercial Systems roadmap, encompassing CRM (Salesforce) and other technology systems and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Commercial Strategy, Revenue Management, Sales Leadership, and other cross-functional teams to translate business needs into practical technology solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in build vs. buy evaluations for new tool investments, summarizing trade-offs for leadership review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure platforms are well-documented, integrated, and maintained for long-term sustainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Salesforce Platform Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ongoing development, configuration, and optimization of the Salesforce platform to support field sales effectiveness and optimization of Commercial effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead requirements gathering, solution design, user story development, and UAT for Salesforce workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own release management, platform documentation, and end-user training to ensure adoption and data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the JLI IT team to ensure sound integrations between Salesforce and adjacent platforms including ERP, data warehouses, and third-party analytics tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Tool Development &amp;amp; Delivery Oversight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design and delivery of custom-built internal tools where Commercial needs exceed off-the-shelf capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define technical requirements and coordinate with development teams or vendors to execute software builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish engineering standards, QA processes, and release cadences for internally developed tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure custom solutions integrate with the broader commercial systems ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AI Roadmap for Commercial&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain the AI roadmap for the Commercial function, identifying high-value use cases such as account prioritization, lead and opportunity scoring, rep coaching, territory planning, content generation, and field reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT, Data, and external vendors to evaluate AI solutions; lead pilots and define the criteria for scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion responsible adoption — building field confidence, managing change, measuring impact, and iterating based on user feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Stakeholder Collaboration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Commercial teams and functional partners to identify systems needs and maintain alignment on priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate technical concepts into clear business language for management audiences; translate business requirements into technical specifications for development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with PMO and Commercial Planning functions to align systems delivery with commercial initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Team &amp;amp; Vendor Coordination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a small team of Salesforce administrators and systems analysts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with external development vendors, system integrators, and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track platform budgets, project milestones, and delivery progress across active workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform related duties as assigned, within your scope of practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PERSONAL AND PROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are open to candidates from two primary backgrounds — what matters most is the combination of systems thinking, collaborative leadership, and a track record of delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Process Architecture / Operations Track&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in sales operations, revenue operations, commercial strategy, or management consulting with a strong technology component&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong process design skills — ability to map and operationalize commercial workflows across organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define requirements for and oversee delivery of systems projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating with technical development teams or vendors against a defined roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid fluency with enterprise platforms (CRM, ERP, BI/analytics) and ability to support technology evaluation decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Technical / Engineering Track&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in software engineering, commercial systems development, or enterprise technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building or supporting full-stack or enterprise applications in a commercial context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Salesforce and the ability to contribute to platform-level design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to ERP systems (SAP, Oracle, NetSuite) and cross-platform integrations&lt;/li&gt;
